\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang2057\langfe1033\langfenp1033\insrsid6513979\charrsid983060 
Evidence from a Microsoft study indicates that MFA can substantially reduce the risk of account compromise, although its effectiveness depends on the methods of authentication used. A Microsoft study analysed suspicious activity involving Microsoft Azure 
Active Directory accounts between April and September 2022, the researchers estimated that MFA reduced the risk of account compromise by 99.22% across the overall population and by 98.56% for accounts where credentials had been leaked and compromised comp
letely. The study also found that authenticator applications performed better than SMS authentication}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\lang2057\langfe1033\langfenp1033\insrsid6513979\charrsid983060  }{\field{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
