\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang2057\langfe1033\langfenp1033\insrsid6513979\charrsid983060 
This study provides useful evidence because it examined real account activity rather than relying solely on theoretical security models. However, the results should not be interpreted as meaning that every MFA implementation prevents 99.22% of attacks. Ra
ther the research examined Microsoft's commercial account environment and a specific period of suspicious activity, so the results may not directly correlate and represent every organisation, individual or type of MFA.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid10976062\charrsid983060 
