\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang2057\langfe1033\langfenp1033\insrsid6513979\charrsid983060 
Despite its weaknesses, security organisations still continue to recommend enabling MFA, including SMS based MFA when stronger alternatives are unavailable. This is because SMS MFA still provides that additional barrier compared with the classic password 
only authentication method. The UK NCSC explicitly states that SMS is not the most secure type of 2 step verification but still provides a significant advantage over not using a second factor at all }{\field{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
