Overall, MFA significantly strengthens account security by requiring evidence from multiple authentication factors. Research from Microsoft and Google demonstrates that MFA can substantially reduce account compromise, but the level of protection varies ac
cording to the authentication method. SMS provides useful and the most simple and easy to deploy protection against many automated and credential based attacks but remains vulnerable to more advanced techniques such as SIM swapping and phishing. Authentic
a
tor applications generally provide stronger protection, while FIDO2 security keys provide phishing resistant authentication. Consequently, organisations should implement MFA whenever possible while selecting authentication methods according to the securit
y requirements, usability needs and risks associated with their systems.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10976062\charrsid983060 
